course: dictionary
lesson: 3414
title: Expose: uncover, reveal or leave open
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Expose is a verb, so it shows an action: you can expose something, and someone can expose a secret. Its main meanings are to uncover something so it can be seen, to leave something open to danger or weather, or to show the truth about a bad person.
explain: Context tells you which meaning fits. «Do not expose skin to strong sun» means do not leave your skin unprotected, because the sun can harm it. In a story, if a liar is exposed, the truth about them has been shown to everyone.
explain: Read this from the Proverbs: «have a quiet word in private rather than exposing him». Here the friend's boast is harmless, so exposing him means making his boast known to everyone in a way that shames him. The writer says a quiet word in private is kinder.
fact: Expose means to uncover something so it can be seen.
fact: Expose can also mean to leave someone or something without protection from danger, weather or sunlight, as in «exposed skin».
fact: Expose can mean to show the truth about a bad person or a secret.
fact: In photography, to expose a film or sensor means to let light reach it.
fact: The forms are expose, exposes, exposed and exposing.
exercise: «Do not expose skin to strong sun.» What does expose mean here? | Cover up with a hat | Shine a torch on | *Leave without protection from the sun | Wash with cold water
exercise: «Have a quiet word in private rather than exposing him.» What does exposing him mean? | Sending him home early | Giving him a present | *Making his boast known to everyone | Whispering to him in private
exercise: The teacher wants to expose the children to music. What does she want? | To stop them hearing any music | To lock the music room | *To give them new experiences of music | To sell them instruments
test: «The detective exposed the liar in front of the whole class.» What does exposed mean? | *Showed the truth about him | Hid him behind the door | Gave him a prize | Made him fall asleep
test: In a camera, exposing the film means what? | Throwing the film away | *Letting light reach the film | Covering the lens | Keeping it dry in a bag
exam: The workers exposed the old pipes when they dug up the road. What does exposed mean? | *Uncovered so they could be seen | Buried deeper under the soil | Painted bright red | Lost for ever
